      "rev_n_1_e04bf5_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_1_e04bf5_1",
        "node_id": "n_1_e04bf5",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of assigning incremental values starting from the highest rating doesn't satisfy the condition of giving distinct ratings to users with the same minimum required rating. Instead, we should sort the ratings in descending order and assign values based on the relative order of the required ratings, ensuring that users with the same minimum required rating receive the same value.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_1_e04bf5_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_0b3cef11d7",
        "created_at": 1794532165.212085
      },
      "rev_n_2_2caeb5_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_2_2caeb5_1",
        "node_id": "n_2_2caeb5",
        "thought_text": "The current approach fails because it doesn't consider the requirement that each user should receive at least their desired rating. The loop should start from the smallest desired rating and assign ratings incrementally, ensuring that each user receives at least their desired rating while maintaining distinct ratings.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
        "replaces_revision_id": "rev_n_2_2caeb5_0",
        "feedback_id": "fb_70123fa3c7",
        "created_at": 1794532185.2891252
      },
      "rev_n_3_584aba_1": {
        "revision_id": "rev_n_3_584aba_1",
        "node_id": "n_3_584aba",
        "thought_text": "The current approach of sorting the ratings and assigning them sequentially doesn't work for all cases. We need to consider the minimum possible rating for each user based on their position in the sorted list and their required minimum rating. This ensures that we maintain the distinctness of ratings while minimizing the total sum.",
        "parent_revision_path_hash": "5740354900026072187",
